---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
import Slider from '../../../components/sim/Slider.astro';
import Checks from '../../../components/sim/Checks.astro';
import Transport from '../../../components/sim/Transport.astro';
import Result from '../../../components/sim/Result.astro';
import Caption from '../../../components/sim/Caption.astro';
import Readout from '../../../components/sim/Readout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="computer-vision"
  title="Boxes and Overlap"
  description="A detector does not hand you one box for one object. It hands you a heap of overlapping guesses with scores on them, and two rules turn that heap into an answer: a number for how much two boxes are the same box, and a procedure that keeps the best and deletes its neighbours. Step through it one decision at a time."
  shortcuts={['run', 'step', 'reset', 'fullscreen']}
>
  <div class="sim">
    <div class="sim-view">
      <div class="sim-stage">
        <canvas
          id="bb"
          width="1000"
          height="500"
          role="img"
          aria-label="A scene with a heap of overlapping candidate boxes, the queue of them ordered by score, and the overlap between the two boxes being compared right now."
        ></canvas>
      </div>
      <Caption
        legend={[
          { label: 'a real object', color: '#f59e0b' },
          { label: 'kept', color: '#34d399' },
          { label: 'deleted for overlapping a better one', color: '#f87171' },
          { label: 'still waiting its turn', color: 'rgba(229,231,235,0.55)' },
        ]}
        hint="Step through the decisions one at a time · click any box to compare it yourself"
      />
      <Result label="After the overlap rule" />
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <Transport step />
      <Slider id="conf" label="Score needed to enter" min={20} max={90} value={45} display="0.45" />
      <Slider id="iou" label="Overlap that counts as the same box" min={5} max={95} value={45} display="0.45" />
      <Checks
        items={[
          { id: 'dead', label: 'Keep the deleted boxes on screen', checked: true },
          { id: 'marks', label: 'Mark each kept box right or wrong', checked: true },
        ]}
      />
      <Readout
        title="Values"
        rows={[
          { id: 'r-cand', label: 'boxes in the heap' },
          { id: 'r-kept', label: 'kept' },
          { id: 'r-dead', label: 'deleted' },
          { id: 'r-found', label: 'objects found' },
          { id: 'r-false', label: 'false alarms' },
          { id: 'r-fit', label: 'how well they sit' },
          { id: 'r-iou', label: 'overlap being judged' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      This is what a detector actually returns: not three boxes for three robots
      but a <b>heap</b> of overlapping guesses, each with a score. Every object
      answers at several nearby windows, and a few places answer that had no
      object in them at all.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Intersection over union</b> is the one number that says how much two
      boxes are the same box. The right-hand panel draws it: the shaded part over
      the whole outlined part. It is 1 when they coincide, 0 when they miss each
      other entirely, and it does not care how big the boxes are, which is the
      reason this ratio is used rather than the overlap on its own.
    </li>
    <li>
      Press <b>Step</b>. The rule is three lines: take the highest-scoring box
      left, keep it, and delete everything overlapping it by more than the
      threshold. Repeat until nothing is left. That is non-maximum suppression,
      and every decision you step through is one comparison against one kept box.
    </li>
    <li>
      Drag <b>the overlap that counts as the same box</b> up to 0.8 and every
      robot keeps a stack of three or four, because only near-identical boxes
      still count as the same box. Drag it down to 0.3 and the count barely
      moves, but <b>how well they sit</b> in the panel falls from 0.93 to 0.87:
      a well-placed box beside the winner is now deleted for merely touching it,
      and something worse survives in its place.
    </li>
    <li>
      One robot is standing in front of another, and their two real boxes already
      share a third of their area. That is the reason the overlap cannot simply
      be set low: the same number has to mean "another guess at this robot" and
      "a different robot standing behind it", and no value does both. Crowds are
      where this rule fails, and it fails silently.
    </li>
    <li>
      The order is by <b>score</b>, not by how well the box fits. Watch a
      well-placed box get deleted by a worse-fitting one that happened to score
      higher: the rule has no idea which box is the better outline, it only knows
      which number is larger.
    </li>
    <li>
      Lower <b>the score needed to enter</b> and the heap grows with rubbish that
      the rule then has to clean up. The two knobs pull against each other: a low
      bar finds every object and invents some, a high bar invents nothing and
      misses the faint ones.
    </li>
    <li>
      The same ratio grades the result. A kept box counts as correct when it
      overlaps a real object by <b>0.5 or more</b>, and there is nothing physical
      about 0.5: it is a convention, and every detection score you have ever read
      was computed against a number somebody chose.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas, makeText } from '../../../lib/sim';
  import { equation } from '../../../lib/equation';
  import { stageInk, roundRect } from '../../../lib/draw';
  import { el, slider, check, transport, result, readout } from '../../../lib/panel';

  const TRUTH = '#f59e0b', KEEP = '#34d399', DEAD = '#f87171', WAIT = '#e5e7eb';
  const IMG = 180;
  const MATCH = 0.5; // what the grading convention calls a hit

  // --- the scene, drawn rather than photographed -----------------------------
  const INK = '#2a2a33';
  const BOTS = [
    { x: 16, y: 20, s: 1 },
    { x: 100, y: 30, s: 0.85 },
    { x: 48, y: 104, s: 1.15 },
    // a small one standing in front of the first, so two real objects share
    // most of a box and the rule has to decide whether they are one thing
    { x: 36, y: 40, s: 0.62 },
  ];
  function robot(c: CanvasRenderingContext2D, b: { x: number; y: number; s: number }) {
    c.save();
    c.translate(b.x, b.y);
    c.scale(b.s, b.s);
    c.lineWidth = 2;
    c.strokeStyle = INK;
    c.beginPath();
    c.moveTo(42, 2);
    c.lineTo(48, -12);
    c.stroke();
    c.beginPath();
    c.arc(48, -14, 3.4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    c.fillStyle = '#e2725b';
    c.fill();
    c.stroke();
    roundRect(c, 0, 0, 52, 46, 9);
    c.fillStyle = '#c9cfdb';
    c.fill();
    c.stroke();
    for (const ex of [15, 37]) {
      c.beginPath();
      c.arc(ex, 17, 8, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      c.fillStyle = '#ffffff';
      c.fill();
      c.stroke();
      c.beginPath();
      c.arc(ex + 2.6, 17, 4.2, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      c.fillStyle = INK;
      c.fill();
    }
    c.fillStyle = INK;
    for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) c.fillRect(13 + i * 6, 33, 4, 5);
    c.restore();
  }
  const scene = document.createElement('canvas');
  scene.width = IMG;
  scene.height = IMG;
  (() => {
    const c = scene.getContext('2d')!;
    c.fillStyle = '#ece7dc';
    c.fillRect(0, 0, IMG, IMG);
    for (const b of BOTS) robot(c, b);
  })();

  type Box = { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number };
  /** Where the robots really are, which the detector does not know. */
  const REAL: Box[] = BOTS.map((b) => ({ x: b.x - 2, y: b.y - 2, w: 56 * b.s, h: 50 * b.s }));

  // --- the heap a detector would have produced -------------------------------
  function mulberry32(a: number) {
    return () => {
      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;
      let t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a);
      t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;
      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;
    };
  }
  type Cand = Box & { v: number; state: number; by: number; ok: boolean; fit: number };
  const HEAP: Cand[] = (() => {
    const r = mulberry32(20260911);
    const out: Cand[] = [];
    REAL.forEach((t, i) => {
      // several windows answer for the same object, each a little off
      const n = 4 + (i % 2);
      for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) {
        const j = k === 0 ? 0.04 : 0.08 + 0.17 * r();
        const sx = 1 + (r() - 0.5) * j * 2, sy = 1 + (r() - 0.5) * j * 2;
        const w = t.w * sx, h = t.h * sy;
        const x = t.x + (r() - 0.5) * j * t.w * 1.6, y = t.y + (r() - 0.5) * j * t.h * 1.6;
        // the score is only loosely tied to how well the box sits, which is
        // true of real detectors and is what makes the ordering interesting
        out.push({ x, y, w, h, v: Math.max(0.31, 0.97 - j * 1.6 + (r() - 0.5) * 0.2), state: 0, by: -1, ok: false, fit: 0 });
      }
    });
    // and a few places answer that hold no robot at all
    for (const [x, y, w, h, v] of [
      [118, 124, 46, 40, 0.58], [8, 150, 40, 26, 0.41], [132, 4, 38, 30, 0.49], [70, 64, 34, 30, 0.44],
    ] as number[][])
      out.push({ x, y, w, h, v, state: 0, by: -1, ok: false, fit: 0 });
    return out.sort((a, b) => b.v - a.v);
  })();

  const inter = (a: Box, b: Box) =>
    Math.max(0, Math.min(a.x + a.w, b.x + b.w) - Math.max(a.x, b.x)) *
    Math.max(0, Math.min(a.y + a.h, b.y + b.h) - Math.max(a.y, b.y));
  const iou = (a: Box, b: Box) => {
    const i = inter(a, b);
    return i / (a.w * a.h + b.w * b.h - i);
  };

  // --- the rule, one decision at a time --------------------------------------
  // state: 0 waiting, 1 kept, 2 deleted, 3 never entered (below the score bar)
  const state = { conf: 0.45, iou: 0.45, dead: true, marks: true, running: false };
  let queue: Cand[] = [];
  let at = 0; // how far down the queue the rule has got
  /** The comparison the last decision turned on. */
  let judged: { a: Cand; b: Cand | null; v: number; killed: boolean } | null = null;
  let inspect: Cand | null = null;

  function reset() {
    for (const c of HEAP) {
      c.state = c.v >= state.conf ? 0 : 3;
      c.by = -1;
      c.ok = false;
      c.fit = 0;
    }
    queue = HEAP.filter((c) => c.state === 0);
    at = 0;
    judged = null;
    inspect = null;
  }
  /** Take the next box: keep it, or delete it for overlapping a better one. */
  function step() {
    if (at >= queue.length) return false;
    const c = queue[at++];
    let worst: Cand | null = null, worstV = -1;
    for (const k of queue) {
      if (k.state !== 1) continue;
      const v = iou(c, k);
      if (v > worstV) {
        worstV = v;
        worst = k;
      }
    }
    const killed = worst !== null && worstV > state.iou;
    c.state = killed ? 2 : 1;
    if (killed) c.by = queue.indexOf(worst!);
    judged = { a: c, b: worst, v: Math.max(0, worstV), killed };
    grade();
    return true;
  }
  function runAll() {
    while (step());
  }
  /** A kept box is right when it covers a real object by half or more. */
  function grade() {
    const taken = new Set<number>();
    for (const c of queue) {
      if (c.state !== 1) continue;
      c.ok = false;
      c.fit = 0;
      let best = -1, bestV = MATCH;
      REAL.forEach((t, i) => {
        if (taken.has(i)) return;
        const v = iou(c, t);
        if (v >= bestV) {
          bestV = v;
          best = i;
        }
      });
      if (best >= 0) {
        taken.add(best);
        c.ok = true;
        c.fit = bestV;
      }
    }
    return taken.size;
  }

  // --- drawing ---------------------------------------------------------------
  const canvas = el('bb') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => draw());
  const { ink, inv } = stageInk(canvas);
  const { label } = makeText(ctx, ink);
  const setEq = equation();
  const setResult = result();
  const setRows = readout();

  const SC = { x: 36, y: 104, s: 356 };
  const OV = { x: 604, y: 104, s: 356 };
  const QX = 420, QW = 156;

  function panel(x: number, y: number, s: number) {
    ctx.save();
    ctx.shadowColor = 'rgba(0,0,0,0.4)';
    ctx.shadowBlur = 14;
    ctx.shadowOffsetY = 3;
    ctx.fillStyle = inv(0.55);
    roundRect(ctx, x, y, s, s, 12);
    ctx.fill();
    ctx.restore();
    ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.18);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    roundRect(ctx, x + 0.5, y + 0.5, s - 1, s - 1, 12);
    ctx.stroke();
  }
  const u = () => SC.s / IMG;
  function rect(b: Box, colour: string, width: number, dash?: number[]) {
    const k = u();
    if (dash) ctx.setLineDash(dash);
    ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(0,0,0,0.45)';
    ctx.lineWidth = width + 1.4;
    ctx.strokeRect(SC.x + b.x * k, SC.y + b.y * k, b.w * k, b.h * k);
    ctx.strokeStyle = colour;
    ctx.lineWidth = width;
    ctx.strokeRect(SC.x + b.x * k, SC.y + b.y * k, b.w * k, b.h * k);
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
  }

  function scenePanel() {
    const kept = queue.filter((c) => c.state === 1);
    label('the heap, and what is left of it', SC.x, SC.y - 30, 0.55, 'left', 13);
    label(`${at} of ${queue.length} decided`, SC.x, SC.y - 12, 0.32, 'left', 11);
    panel(SC.x, SC.y, SC.s);
    ctx.save();
    roundRect(ctx, SC.x, SC.y, SC.s, SC.s, 12);
    ctx.clip();
    ctx.drawImage(scene, SC.x, SC.y, SC.s, SC.s);
    for (const t of REAL) rect(t, `${TRUTH}aa`, 1.4, [4, 4]);
    for (const c of queue) {
      if (c.state === 0) rect(c, 'rgba(229,231,235,0.55)', 1);
      else if (c.state === 2 && state.dead) rect(c, `${DEAD}66`, 1, [3, 3]);
    }
    for (const c of queue)
      if (c.state === 1) {
        rect(c, KEEP, 2);
        const k = u();
        if (state.marks)
          label(c.ok ? '✓' : '✗', SC.x + c.x * k + 3, SC.y + c.y * k + 14, 1, 'left', 13, c.ok ? KEEP : DEAD);
      }
    const show = inspect ?? judged?.a;
    if (show) rect(show, WAIT, 2.2);
    ctx.restore();
  }

  /** The queue, in the order the rule works through it. */
  function queuePanel() {
    label('by score', QX + QW / 2, SC.y - 30, 0.55, 'center', 13);
    label('the order asked', QX + QW / 2, SC.y - 12, 0.32, 'center', 11);
    const rh = Math.min(15, SC.s / Math.max(1, queue.length));
    queue.forEach((c, i) => {
      const y = SC.y + i * rh;
      const now = c === (inspect ?? judged?.a);
      const colour = c.state === 1 ? KEEP : c.state === 2 ? DEAD : ink(0.35);
      ctx.fillStyle = i < at ? ink(0.06) : 'transparent';
      if (i < at) ctx.fillRect(QX, y, QW, rh - 1);
      ctx.fillStyle = c.state === 1 ? KEEP : c.state === 2 ? `${DEAD}cc` : ink(0.28);
      ctx.fillRect(QX + 26, y + 2, (QW - 60) * c.v, rh - 5);
      label(c.v.toFixed(2), QX, y + rh - 3, now ? 0.95 : 0.5, 'left', 10, now ? WAIT : undefined);
      label(c.state === 1 ? 'keep' : c.state === 2 ? 'gone' : '·', QX + QW - 2, y + rh - 3, now ? 0.95 : 0.55, 'right', 10, colour);
      if (now) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = WAIT;
        ctx.lineWidth = 1;
        ctx.strokeRect(QX - 2.5, y + 0.5, QW + 4, rh - 1);
      }
    });
  }

  /** The two boxes the current decision is about, drawn big. */
  function overlapPanel() {
    label('how much the same box', OV.x, OV.y - 30, 0.55, 'left', 13);
    const j = inspect ? { a: inspect, b: bestKeptAgainst(inspect), v: 0, killed: false } : judged;
    if (j && j.b) j.v = iou(j.a, j.b);
    label(
      j && j.b ? 'the box being judged, against the kept one' : 'nothing to compare yet',
      OV.x, OV.y - 12, 0.32, 'left', 11
    );
    panel(OV.x, OV.y, OV.s);
    if (!j || !j.b) return;
    const a = j.a, b = j.b;
    const lo = { x: Math.min(a.x, b.x), y: Math.min(a.y, b.y) };
    const hi = { x: Math.max(a.x + a.w, b.x + b.w), y: Math.max(a.y + a.h, b.y + b.h) };
    const span = Math.max(hi.x - lo.x, hi.y - lo.y) * 1.25;
    const k = (OV.s - 80) / span;
    const ox = OV.x + OV.s / 2 - ((lo.x + hi.x) / 2) * k, oy = OV.y + OV.s / 2 - 14 - ((lo.y + hi.y) / 2) * k;
    const put = (r: Box) => ({ x: ox + r.x * k, y: oy + r.y * k, w: r.w * k, h: r.h * k });
    const A = put(a), B = put(b);
    // the shared part, and the part they cover between them
    const ix = Math.max(A.x, B.x), iy = Math.max(A.y, B.y);
    const iw = Math.min(A.x + A.w, B.x + B.w) - ix, ih = Math.min(A.y + A.h, B.y + B.h) - iy;
    ctx.save();
    roundRect(ctx, OV.x, OV.y, OV.s, OV.s, 12);
    ctx.clip();
    ctx.fillStyle = `${KEEP}22`;
    ctx.fillRect(B.x, B.y, B.w, B.h);
    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(229,231,235,0.10)';
    ctx.fillRect(A.x, A.y, A.w, A.h);
    if (iw > 0 && ih > 0) {
      ctx.fillStyle = `${TRUTH}66`;
      ctx.fillRect(ix, iy, iw, ih);
    }
    ctx.strokeStyle = KEEP;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.strokeRect(B.x, B.y, B.w, B.h);
    ctx.strokeStyle = WAIT;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.setLineDash([5, 3]);
    ctx.strokeRect(A.x, A.y, A.w, A.h);
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    ctx.restore();
    label('the kept one', B.x + 4, B.y - 6, 0.9, 'left', 11, KEEP);
    label('the one being judged', A.x + 4, A.y + A.h + 14, 0.9, 'left', 11, WAIT);
    const v = iou(a, b);
    label(`shared ${Math.round(inter(a, b))} ÷ covered ${Math.round(a.w * a.h + b.w * b.h - inter(a, b))} = ${v.toFixed(2)}`, OV.x + OV.s / 2, OV.y + OV.s - 34, 0.5, 'center', 12, TRUTH);
    label(
      v > state.iou ? `${v.toFixed(2)} is over ${state.iou.toFixed(2)}, so it goes` : `${v.toFixed(2)} is under ${state.iou.toFixed(2)}, so it stays`,
      OV.x + OV.s / 2, OV.y + OV.s - 14, 0.9, 'center', 12.5, v > state.iou ? DEAD : KEEP
    );
  }
  const bestKeptAgainst = (c: Cand) => {
    let best: Cand | null = null, bv = -1;
    for (const k of queue) {
      if (k.state !== 1 || k === c) continue;
      const v = iou(c, k);
      if (v > bv) {
        bv = v;
        best = k;
      }
    }
    return best;
  };

  function draw() {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    scenePanel();
    queuePanel();
    overlapPanel();

    const kept = queue.filter((c) => c.state === 1);
    const found = kept.filter((c) => c.ok).length;
    const j = inspect ? { a: inspect, b: bestKeptAgainst(inspect) } : judged;
    const v = j && j.b ? iou(j.a, j.b) : -1;
    setEq({
      rule: [
        ['\\text{IoU}(A,B) = \\dfrac{|A \\cap B|}{|A \\cup B|}', TRUTH],
        '\\qquad',
        ['\\text{keep if } \\max_k \\text{IoU} \\le t', KEEP],
      ],
      live: [
        [`t = ${state.iou.toFixed(2)}`, KEEP],
        v >= 0 ? [`\\quad \\text{this pair} = ${v.toFixed(2)}`, TRUTH] : '',
        [`\\quad ${kept.length} \\text{ kept of } ${queue.length}`, KEEP],
      ],
    });
    setRows({
      'r-cand': String(queue.length),
      'r-kept': String(kept.length),
      'r-dead': String(queue.filter((c) => c.state === 2).length),
      'r-found': `${found} of ${REAL.length}`,
      'r-false': String(kept.length - found),
      'r-fit': found ? (kept.reduce((a, c) => a + c.fit, 0) / found).toFixed(3) : '—',
      'r-iou': v >= 0 ? v.toFixed(3) : '—',
    });
    const done = at >= queue.length;
    setResult({
      value: `${kept.length} box${kept.length === 1 ? '' : 'es'}`,
      colour: kept.length === REAL.length && found === REAL.length ? KEEP : TRUTH,
      status: `${queue.length} in the heap · ${at} decided · ${found} of ${REAL.length} robots found, ${kept.length - found} false alarm${kept.length - found === 1 ? '' : 's'} · overlap allowed ${state.iou.toFixed(2)}`,
      note: !done
        ? 'The rule has not finished. Every box still waiting will be kept or deleted by exactly one comparison against the boxes already kept.'
        : state.iou < 0.15
          ? 'At this overlap almost anything counts as the same box, so boxes on genuinely different robots delete each other and objects go missing.'
          : state.iou > 0.6
            ? 'At this overlap only near-identical boxes count as the same, so each robot keeps a small stack of its own guesses and the count comes out too high.'
            : found === REAL.length && kept.length === REAL.length
              ? 'One box per robot and nothing else, which is what the two rules are for. Neither of them knows anything about robots.'
              : found === REAL.length
                ? 'Every robot has exactly one box, and the extras are boxes on places where there is no robot at all. No overlap rule can remove those, because they overlap nothing: only the score can.'
                : 'Some robots have no box at all now. Between them, the score needed to enter and the overlap allowed have thrown away every guess at them.',
    });
  }

  // --- controls --------------------------------------------------------------
  canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
    const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
    const x = ((e.clientX - r.left) / r.width) * W, y = ((e.clientY - r.top) / r.height) * H;
    if (x < SC.x || x > SC.x + SC.s || y < SC.y || y > SC.y + SC.s) return;
    const ix = ((x - SC.x) / SC.s) * IMG, iy = ((y - SC.y) / SC.s) * IMG;
    let pick: Cand | null = null, area = Infinity;
    for (const c of queue)
      if (ix >= c.x && ix <= c.x + c.w && iy >= c.y && iy <= c.y + c.h && c.w * c.h < area) {
        area = c.w * c.h;
        pick = c;
      }
    inspect = pick === inspect ? null : pick;
    draw();
  });

  /** Changing a rule re-runs it, so the page always shows a finished answer. */
  function redo() {
    state.running = false;
    controls.setRunning(false);
    reset();
    runAll();
    inspect = queue.find((c) => c.state === 2) ?? null;
    draw();
  }
  slider('conf', (v) => { state.conf = v / 100; redo(); }, (v) => (v / 100).toFixed(2));
  slider('iou', (v) => { state.iou = v / 100; redo(); }, (v) => (v / 100).toFixed(2));
  check('dead', (on) => { state.dead = on; draw(); });
  check('marks', (on) => { state.marks = on; draw(); });

  const controls = transport({
    onRun: (running) => {
      if (running && at >= queue.length) reset();
      state.running = running;
    },
    onStep: () => {
      if (at >= queue.length) reset();
      inspect = null;
      step();
      draw();
    },
    onReset: () => {
      state.running = false;
      controls.setRunning(false);
      reset();
      draw();
    },
  });

  let last = 0;
  function frame(t: number) {
    if (state.running && t - last > 420) {
      last = t;
      inspect = null;
      if (!step()) {
        state.running = false;
        controls.setRunning(false);
      }
      draw();
    }
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }

  reset();
  runAll();
  // open on a decision that turned on a real overlap rather than the last one
  inspect = queue.find((c) => c.state === 2) ?? null;
  draw();
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
</script>

<style>
  #bb {
    cursor: pointer;
  }
</style>
